#  VERSION holds what the release buttons read to name the version each
#  press publishes. It is not the currently released version: that lives
#  in pyproject.toml and src/worktoy/__init__.py, both stamped from here at
#  publish time. The state machine reading it is release_state.py.
#
#  MAJOR and MINOR hold the line of the last full release, and MICRO the
#  next micro after it, so the last full release is MAJOR.MINOR.(MICRO-1).
#  LEVEL holds the level locked for the next release: none, micro, minor or
#  major. Each level leads to a target counted from the last full release:
#    micro -> MAJOR.MINOR.MICRO
#    minor -> MAJOR.(MINOR+1).0
#    major -> (MAJOR+1).0.0
#  DEV and RC hold the next dev and rc number of the target of LEVEL.
#
#  LEVEL=none: no cycle is open. Only a dev button runs; it needs its
#    safety, locks its level and publishes the dev0 of its target.
#  A level locked, RC=0: a dev cycle is open. A dev press of the locked
#    level publishes the next devN with no safety; one of a higher level
#    needs its safety, relocks and publishes its dev0. The rc of the locked
#    level needs its safety and publishes rc0, closing the dev cycle.
#  A level locked, RC above 0: an rc cycle is open. The rc of the locked
#    level publishes the next rcN with no safety; its lts needs its safety,
#    publishes the release and sets LEVEL back to none.
#  Every other press is refused in the first job of its workflow.
MAJOR=1
MINOR=1
MICRO=1
RC=0
DEV=1
LEVEL=minor
